{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RLSA-2026:102195","published":"2026-11-24T12:07:05.846210Z","modified":"2026-11-24T12:30:02.155967165Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-106552","CVE-2026-106553","CVE-2026-106582","CVE-2026-106583","CVE-2026-106585"],"summary":"Moderate: openssh security, bug fix, and enhancement update","details":"OpenSSH is an SSH protocol implementation supported by a number of Linux, UNIX, and similar operating systems. It includes the core files necessary for both the OpenSSH client and server.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* openssh: openssh: Information disclosure via shared compression side-channel (CVE-2026-106582)\n\n* openssh: openssh: Arbitrary file write via directory traversal during sftp recursive copy (CVE-2026-106552)\n\n* openssh: OpenSSH: Credential disclosure via failed GSSAPI authentication (CVE-2026-106553)\n\n* openssh: openssh: Denial of service via oversized decompressed packets (CVE-2026-106585)\n\n* openssh: openssh: Command injection via unvalidated command-line username (CVE-2026-106583)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Cannot use IdentititesOnly=yes + PKCS#11 URI in IdentityFile anymore [rhel-10.3.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-288515)\n\n* ssh-copy-id fails to Rocky Linux 10  [rhel-10.3.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-288521)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"openssh-debuginfo","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/openssh-debuginfo?distro=rocky-linux-10&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:9.9p1-34.el10_3.rocky.0.1"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"BaseOS"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:102195.json"}},{"package":{"name":"openssh-keysign","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/openssh-keysign?distro=rocky-linux-10&epoc